<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Georg Büchner</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1813–1837</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Georg Büchner was a German dramatist, revolutionary and scientist, born near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/darmstadt">Darmstadt</a> in the Grand Duchy of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hesse">Hesse</a>. In 1834 he wrote the revolutionary pamphlet <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/der-hessische-landbote">Der Hessische Landbote</a> and then fled abroad. In a few years he wrote the plays <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dantons-death">Danton's Death</a>, Leonce and Lena and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/woyzeck">Woyzeck</a> and the story Lenz, before dying of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/typhus">typhus</a> in Zurich at the age of twenty-three.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/georg-buchner.jpg" alt="Georg Büchner" width="320" height="378" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Georg Büchner · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Georg_B%C3%BCchner_-_Franzos-Werkausgabe_!04.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
